PART 2: final Keyword in Java
8. What is final?
final means cannot be changed.

Used with:
Variables
Methods
Classes

Interview one-liner
“Final prevents modification, overriding, or inheritance.”

9. Final Variable
  Example
  public class Test {
      public static void main(String[] args) {
          final int x = 10;
          // x = 20; ❌
          System.out.println(x);
      }
  }
  
  Output
  10

10. Final Reference Variable (Very Important)
  import java.util.*;
  
  public class Test {
      public static void main(String[] args) {
          final List<String> list = new ArrayList<>();
          list.add("Java");
          list.add("Spring");
  
          System.out.println(list);
  
          // list = new ArrayList<>(); ❌
      }
  }
  
  Output
  [Java, Spring]
👉 Reference is final, object is mutable

11. Blank Final Variable
  class Demo {
      final int x;
  
      Demo(int value) {
          x = value;
      }
  
      void show() {
          System.out.println(x);
      }
  }
  
  public class Test {
      public static void main(String[] args) {
          new Demo(50).show();
      }
  }
  
  Output
  50

12. Final Method
class Parent {
    final void show() {
        System.out.println("Parent method");
    }
}

class Child extends Parent {
    // void show() {} ❌
}

public class Test {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        new Child().show();
    }
}

Output
Parent method

👉 Prevents overriding
👉 Used for security & consistency

13. Final Class
  final class Utility {
      static void help() {
          System.out.println("Utility method");
      }
  }
  
  public class Test {
      public static void main(String[] args) {
          Utility.help();
      }
  }
  
  Output
  Utility method
  
❌ Cannot extend final class
✔ String, wrapper classes are final

14. static final (Constant Pattern)
  class Constants {
      public static final int MAX_USERS = 100;
  }
  
  public class Test {
      public static void main(String[] args) {
          System.out.println(Constants.MAX_USERS);
      }
  }
  
  Output
  100

Why static final?
  One copy
  Immutable
  Compile-time constant

15. Static vs Final (🔥 Must-Remember)
| Feature        | static             | final        |
| -------------- | ------------------ | ------------ |
| Belongs to     | Class              | Restriction  |
| Change allowed | Yes                | No           |
| Polymorphism   | ❌                  | ❌            |
| Memory         | Method Area        | Depends      |
| Common use     | Utility, constants | Immutability |

16. static & final in Interfaces
interface Test {
    int X = 10; // public static final
}

public class Demo {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println(Test.X);
    }
}

Output
10

17. JVM / Memory Perspective
  Static members → Method Area
  Instance members → Heap
  static final primitives → inlined at compile time
  Final methods → not overridden → faster dispatch

18. static & final in Spring Boot (🔥 Important)
Static – Avoid in Beans
❌ Autowiring static fields
❌ Stateful static variables
✔ Use static for:
  Constants
  Utility classes
  
Final – Highly Recommended
@Service
class UserService {
    private final Repo repo;

    UserService(Repo repo) {
        this.repo = repo;
    }
}

✔ Thread-safe
✔ Encourages immutability
✔ Best practice in Spring

19. Common Tricky Interview Questions
Q1. Can static methods be overridden?
❌ No (method hiding)

Q2. Can final methods be overloaded?
✅ Yes

Q3. Does final make object immutable?
❌ No (design matters)

Q4. Why String is final?
Security, immutability, caching

Q5. Can constructor be static or final?
❌ No

20. Interview One-Liners (Use These)
“Static belongs to class, final restricts change.”
“Static methods don’t support runtime polymorphism.”
“Final helps achieve immutability and security.”

21. Interview Closing Statement
“Proper use of static and final improves performance, safety, and design clarity, which is essential for scalable Spring Boot applications.”
